# Charts and data

<h2 id="wg-070">Name the measured quantity</h2>

Say what is measured, not just the number. Power and energy are different.

<%= example('wg-data-meaning') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Electricity: 4.62 | Energy used today: 4.62kWh |
| Usage: 420 | Power now: 420W |

<h2 id="wg-071">Keep meaningful precision</h2>

Round only as far as the decision allows. Do not show more digits than the sensor measures.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| 19.4372°C | 19.4°C |
| 0kWh (rounded from 0.004kWh) | 0.004kWh |

<h2 id="wg-072">Respect number and date preferences</h2>

Use the household’s locale. In UK English write “2 June 2026”, not “2nd June” or “06/02/26”. Write times in the household’s clock setting, 5:30pm or 17:30, and use one style on a screen.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| 06/02/26 | 2 June 2026 |
| 1730hrs | 5:30pm |
| 10-11am | 10am to 11am |

<h2 id="wg-073">Keep units with their values</h2>

Write the unit straight after the number, with no space: 21°C, 3,500kg, 4.62kWh. Never show a number without its unit.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Temperature 21 | 21°C |
| 3kW h | 3kWh |

<h2 id="wg-074">Say which time the data covers</h2>

Give the date, time zone and whether a time is the start or the end of an interval.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Usage at 10 | Energy from 10:00 to 11:00 on 11 November 2026 (Europe/London) |

<h2 id="wg-075">Make ambiguous times explicit</h2>

Say “midnight” with the date, or use 11:59pm. Say which day a schedule means when the clocks change.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Heating off at midnight | Heating turns off at 11:59pm on Tuesday 14 June |
| Runs at 01:30 | Runs at 1:30am. On Sunday 25 October 2026 this time happens twice. It runs the first time only. |

<h2 id="wg-076">Keep gaps and real zeros apart</h2>

“No reading” is not 0. Do not add a total over a gap without saying so.

<%= example('wg-data-gaps') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| 10:00: 0.00kWh (no reading) | 10:00: No reading |
| Total: 0.42kWh | Total: 0.42kWh from 2 of 3 hours. The 10:00 reading is missing. |

<h2 id="wg-077">Give charts a text equivalent</h2>

Every chart needs a title, units, the period and a table or sentence with the same data.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| (A line chart with no title) | Hall temperature, 10 to 11 November 2026, in °C. Lowest 17.8 at 03:20, highest 21.5 at 18:05. [View as a table](#) |

<h2 id="wg-078">Compare like with like</h2>

Compare the same period, with the same coverage. Do not claim a saving you did not calculate.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| You used 30% less energy today! | By 12:00 today: 2.1kWh. By 12:00 yesterday: 3.0kWh. |
